From: well83 <well83@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mem: restore CAP_SYS_RAWIO check in open_port()

The Allwinner/Orange Pi BSP commented out the CAP_SYS_RAWIO check, so any
process able to open /dev/mem or /dev/port was not checked for raw I/O
capability. Banana Pi and Walnut Pi BSPs restore it; nothing in the T95
image relies on it (root tools keep CAP_SYS_RAWIO).

---
--- a/drivers/char/mem.c
+++ b/drivers/char/mem.c
@@ -849,8 +849,8 @@
 {
 	int rc;
 
-//	if (!capable(CAP_SYS_RAWIO))
-//		return -EPERM;
+	if (!capable(CAP_SYS_RAWIO))
+		return -EPERM;
 
 	rc = security_locked_down(LOCKDOWN_DEV_MEM);
 	if (rc)
